
1. Python Overview
• Python is a high-level, general-purpose programming language with readable syntax and a large ecosystem.
• Python is widely used in artificial intelligence, machine learning, data science, automation, web development,
and scripting.
• Important concepts include variables, data types, conditions, loops, functions, classes, modules, exceptions,
and file handling.
2. Python Data Types
• Common types include int, float, str, bool, list, tuple, dict, and set.
• Lists store ordered collections, dictionaries store key-value pairs, and sets store unique values.
3. Python Functions
• A function is a reusable block of code that performs a task. It can receive parameters and return a result.
• Functions help divide an application into smaller and easier-to-maintain components.
4. Python File Handling
• Python can read and write files using the built-in open() function.
